+# The Daily Grind
+
+Start the static site with `pnpm start` (default port: 11222).
+
+## CSS architecture
+
+`styles.css` declares the cascade order explicitly:
+
+1. `reset` uses zero-specificity `:where()` selectors.
+2. `tokens` defines the palette, semantic colors, typography, spacing, layout, motion, and stacking values.
+3. `base` defines document defaults and accessible focus styles.
+4. `layout` owns shared containers, grids, and their responsive behavior.
+5. `components` owns named components, nested descendants and states, and scoped section typography.
+6. `utilities` contains final overrides, including reduced motion.
+
+Use semantic tokens in components. Add new component styles inside the components layer, with a class at the root and native nesting for descendants, states, and media queries. `@scope` keeps hero and footer typography local. Keep styling out of HTML and avoid ID selectors and `!important` so the layer order remains predictable.
+
+The stylesheet targets modern browsers supporting native CSS nesting, cascade layers, and `@scope`. It is served directly without a build step.
+
+## Stock photography
+
+Photos are saved locally in `assets/` from Unsplash:
+
+- Hero: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085
+- Maple latte: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1541167760496-1628856ab772
+- Espresso: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1510707577719-ae7c14805e3a
+- Cold brew: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461023058943-07fcbe16d735
+
+## Automated CSS validation
+
+Run `pnpm dlx lightningcss-cli styles.css -o /tmp/daily-grind-validated.css` to parse the stylesheet without adding a project dependency. The generated file is a validation artifact; the site uses the original stylesheet.
